<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE - United Overseas Insurance 1H slips.</title>
<headline>TABLE - United Overseas Insurance 1H slips.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		  (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    1.59   vs    3.59</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   3.90   vs    8.80</p>
<p>    Gross premium income	     17.78   vs   17.86</p>
<p>    Gross investment income	   2.06   vs    1.99</p>
<p>    Profit on investments sale	1.18   vs    1.09</p>
<p>    Non-underwriting income	   3.29   vs    3.11</p>
<p>    Underwriting profit		 2.52   vs    2.46</p>
<p>    Net profit before tax	     2.15   vs    4.85</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.56   vs    1.26</p>
<p>Note - United Overseas Insurance Ltd, part of United Overseas Bank, said gross investment earnings were better than that achieved in the corresponding period last year. But gains were eroded by the high levels of provision for unrealised losses due to a weak stock market and compliance with stringent regulatory requirements for such provisions. It said the insurance market remains soft and very competitive and this was likely to continue in the remaining half of the year.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
